```sql
--Description: To satisfy the original goal—retrieve each molecule (trade_name) linked to the
--             Sanofi / Aventis group and keep only its most recent FDA approval—we:
--               1. Recognise that the literal string “SanofiAventis” is absent; the company appears
--                  with spaces or hyphens (“SANOFI AVENTIS …”, “SANOFI-AVENTIS …”).
--               2. Therefore, we match any applicant_full_name that contains BOTH words “sanofi”
--                  and “aventis” in any order or with any characters between them, using a
--                  case-insensitive regular expression.
--               3. For every matching record, we group by trade_name and keep the latest
--                  approval_date with MAX().
--               4. Finally we sort by trade_name; LIMIT 20 just to inspect a manageable sample.
SELECT
  trade_name,
  MAX(approval_date) AS latest_approval_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
WHERE REGEXP_CONTAINS(LOWER(applicant_full_name), r'sanofi.*aventis|aventis.*sanofi')
GROUP BY trade_name
ORDER BY trade_name
LIMIT 20;
```
